Root cause:
The bug was caused by the incorrect declaration and initialization of the variable `i` in the `FindLength` function. The original code had `int i;` declared at the beginning, which was later used without proper initialization in multiple loops. This could lead to undefined behavior if `i` was used before being assigned a value. The patch corrected this by declaring `i` within the scope of each loop, ensuring it is properly initialized to 0 before use, thus preventing potential logical errors in the loop conditions.
